        {
          "id": "note",
          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## Record and replay\n\nThe **Device** node plays an IQ file back as if it were a radio. Pick a recording on it to start: nothing else here needs hardware.\n\n**Scope** draws the file's spectrum. Scrub the Device node and the waterfall follows.\n\n**Channel** demodulates one signal out of it.\n\n**Baseband scope** shows the channel's constellation and eye. This is how you tell a locked decoder from a guessing one.\n\n**Baseband recorder** keeps just that channel, already down-converted, which is far smaller than the whole band. Record an hour of one channel rather than an hour of the whole window.\n\n**Recorder** with a 30 s **Pre-roll** holds the last seconds of IQ, so Record saves what you just missed. It is wired here to show you where it goes, but it earns its place on a live Device, not on a file you can already scrub.\n\n**Speaker** plays the audio.\n\nPick a radio on the Device instead of a file and this becomes a live receiver that keeps what it hears."
          },
